  "course_description": "Prerequisites: English 101 or 181 and written permission of instructor. Practical introductions to various kinds of media and professional writing. May be repeated for credit when topic varies.",
  "course_notes": "(Libraries, Archives, and Research Methods) - This course introduces students to the theory and practice of research methods in the humanities. Using the ACRLs Framework for Information Literacy, students will learn to evaluate primary and secondary sources, navigate special collections and archives, and cultivate the close reading skills essential to sustained scholarly inquiry. Students will learn about Emory Libraries resources and systems as well as how to use those resources to further their research goals. No prior research experience is required; the course is designed for sophomores and juniors beginning to define their own scholarly interests.",
